solution_md:
 $\textbf{\underline{Solution for (a)} :}$ Let,  $~y=\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} x^x$ Therefore, 
\begin{align*} y=\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} x^x &\implies \log_ey=\log_e(\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} x^x)
&\implies \log_ey=\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} \log_e {x^x}
&\implies \log_ey=\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} \frac{\log_ex}{\frac{1}{x}} 
&\implies \log_ey=\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} \frac{\frac{1}{x}}{-\frac{1}{x^2}}
&\implies \log_ey=-\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} x
&\implies \log_ey=0
&\implies y=\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} x^x=e^0=1 \end{align*}
Therefore, $\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} \Big(x^{x^x}-x^x\Big)$  $=\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} x^{\lim_{x\to 0^{+}} x^x} -
 \lim_{x\to 0^{+}} x^x$  $=0^1-1=~{\boxed{-1}}$ <span style="color:White">oo</span>  :)
