Let  $O'$  be a point such that  $DAO'O$  is a parallelogram. Since,  $OO'=DA=BC$  and  $OO'\parallel DA\parallel BC$ , it follows that  $CBO'O$  is also a parallelogram. Also, we have  $\angle AO'B=\angle DOC$ , since  $AO'\parallel DO$  and  $BO'\parallel CO$ . So,  $\angle AOB+\angle AO'B=180^\circ$  and this implies  $AO'BO$  is cyclic. It is easy to see that  $\triangle O'AB\cong \triangle OBC$ . Hence,   $$ \angle CBO=\angle O'OB=\angle O'AB=\angle ODC. $$   as required.  $\blacksquare$ [asy]
import cse5;
