By Simson line, we have that lines  $O_1O_4,O_3,O_5$  concur at  $O_2$ . Now, let  $\omega_1,\omega_2$  be the circle with diameter  $\overline{AB},\overline{AC}$ , respectively. Then  $O_1,O_4 \in \omega_1$  and  $O_3,O_5 \in \omega_2$ . Now, with directed lengths we have
