\begin{align*}
a^{a+b+c}b^{a+b+c}c^{a+b+c} &\leq a^ab^bc^c
1 &\leq a^ab^bc^c
0 &\leq a\ln a + b\ln b + c\ln c
\end{align*}
Then as the function  $f(x) = x \ln x$  is convex over  $(0, 1)$  we find,
\begin{align*}
f(a) + f(b) + f(c) &\geq 3 f\left( \frac{a+b+c}{3} \right)
& \geq  (a+b+c) \ln \left( \frac{a+b+c}{3} \right)
&\geq 3\ln \left( \frac{a+b+c}{3} \right)
\end{align*}
Then noting that  $\frac{a+b+c}{3} \geq 1$ , and that  $f$  is strictly increasing from  $\left(\frac{1}{e}, \infty \right)$  we find,
\begin{align*}
3 \ln \left( \frac{a+b+c}{3} \right) \geq 3 \ln 1 = 0
\end{align*}**Edit** Oops, I have edited accordingly, simply suffices to note  $a$ ,  $b$  and  $c$  are positive so we don't need convexity at  $x = 0$ .

Multiplying by  $a^ab^bc^c$ , then it suffices to show
\[ 1 = a^{b+c+a} b^{c+a+b} c^{a+b+c} \leq a^ab^bc^c . \]
Taking the ln of both sides, it suffices to show
\begin{align*}
0 = \ln(1) \leq \ln(a^ab^bc^c) = a\ln(a) + b\ln(b) + c\ln(c).
\end{align*}
Notice,  $(x\ln(x))'' = (1+\ln(x))' = \tfrac{1}{x} > 0$ . Hence, by Jensen's,
\begin{align*}
a\ln(a) + b\ln(b) + c\ln(c) \geq \left(\dfrac{a+b+c}{3}\right)\ln\left(\dfrac{a+b+c}{3}\right) \geq \sqrt[3]{abc} \cdot \ln\left(\sqrt[3]{abc}\right) = 1 \cdot \ln(1) \geq 0,
\end{align*}
as desired.

