=PF\cdot PC=PA\cdot PB=\operatorname{Pow}_{\odot(ABD)}(P)$ . This means that  $P$  lies on the radical axis of  $\left\{\odot(CEF),\odot(ABD)\right\}$ . Similarly, we also get that  $Q$  also lies on the radical axis.

So we get that the line  $PQ$  is the radical axis of  $\left\{\odot(ABD),\odot(CEF)\right\}$ . So this gives  $O_1O_2\perp PQ$ .

Now we also have the following.

\begin{align*}
