    Thus,
    \[ \lim_{x\to \alpha_i} \frac{(x-\alpha_i)P'(x)}{P(x)} = 1 + \lim_{x\to \alpha_i} \frac{(x-\alpha_i)Q'(x)}{Q(x)} \]
    Repeating this pattern, inductivly we will get  $r_i = m_i$  where  $m_i$  is the multiplicity of  $\alpha_i$ .
